WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.700
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:04.700 --> 00:08.270
Omoi wa kouya o yuku

00:08.270 --> 00:16.180
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

00:21.350 --> 00:27.990
Yaketsuku hizashi no moto kimi wa nani omou?

00:27.990 --> 00:33.900
Urei no hitomi wa ima nani o utsusu?

00:33.900 --> 00:42.840
Mayowazu ni irareru no nara
step by step tayasui darou

00:42.840 --> 00:47.540
Kaze no you ni

00:47.540 --> 00:50.650
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:50.650 --> 00:54.150
Akatsuki no kouya o yuku

00:54.150 --> 01:00.690
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

01:00.690 --> 01:07.430
Don't be afraid kawaru koto wa
osoreru koto ja nai

01:07.430 --> 01:13.570
Kimi ga kimi de aru naraba will be with you

01:13.570 --> 01:20.240
Odayaka na hi o yume-mite

01:20.240 --> 01:27.550
Michi-naki tabiji wa tsuzuku

01:50.310 --> 01:55.040
Through Blue-eyes' efforts,
we now know the full extent

01:55.040 --> 01:59.450
of Douglas Rosenberg's Project Leviathan.

02:05.620 --> 02:08.790
It is dangerous to leave Ellis at large.

02:08.790 --> 02:11.160
We should dispose of her at once.

02:11.160 --> 02:15.230
However, they are acting on the assumption

02:15.230 --> 02:17.730
that we have obtained this information.

02:17.730 --> 02:22.940
If we act hastily, they may
use that to their advantage.

02:22.940 --> 02:28.080
The Council is leaning towards a
decision that is undesirable for us.

02:28.080 --> 02:31.980
Then, they intend to
allow Ellis to remain alive?

02:31.980 --> 02:35.320
She was originally created at the hands of man.

02:35.320 --> 02:37.750
If a creature born out of
nothing is allowed to live,

02:37.750 --> 02:40.320
she will surely prove to
be the seed of disaster.

02:40.320 --> 02:42.190
I agree.

02:42.190 --> 02:44.590
In the worst case scenario,

02:44.590 --> 02:49.190
we may ignore their decision
and invoke the Law of the Night.

02:51.300 --> 02:55.000
Preparations have already been made.

03:15.620 --> 03:17.830
Nadie? What's going on?!

03:17.830 --> 03:19.790
I'm the one...

03:23.000 --> 03:25.300
...who wants to ask that.

03:34.310 --> 03:35.710
When we arrived in town,

03:35.710 --> 03:39.010
we were suddenly attacked
by weird-looking people!

03:39.010 --> 03:40.650
What did you do?

03:40.650 --> 03:42.550
Nothing.

03:42.550 --> 03:45.650
How many of them? Uh... just lots!

03:45.650 --> 03:47.990
I don't need you to tell me to run, I will...

03:47.990 --> 03:50.090
Hey!

03:50.090 --> 03:52.860
Let's go, Ellis.

03:52.860 --> 03:54.590
Yessir.

04:05.110 --> 04:07.540
It looks like we're in for a long night.

04:19.920 --> 04:23.590
Hey, Ortega! You can hear me, can't you?!

04:23.590 --> 04:27.720
This is our land! How many
times do I have to tell you that?!

04:29.100 --> 04:33.370
It's land you got by currying favor
with some politicians anyway.

04:33.370 --> 04:35.300
Don't park here without permission!

04:35.300 --> 04:37.470
Leave this instant!

04:37.470 --> 04:39.210
Target...

04:39.210 --> 04:41.270
...locked on!

04:44.550 --> 04:46.980
Bang!

04:46.980 --> 04:50.280
That idiot! And he doesn't even work...

05:30.290 --> 05:33.290
Hi, fabulous vehicle you've got there.

05:33.290 --> 05:35.460
Huh? Oh...

06:20.480 --> 06:22.470
That was a mistake.

06:38.530 --> 06:40.160
So?

06:40.160 --> 06:42.600
One faction has overreacted

06:42.600 --> 06:44.770
to the information regarding Project Leviathan

06:44.770 --> 06:47.840
and it seems they have taken action.

06:47.840 --> 06:49.670
I know.

07:06.290 --> 07:09.690
This collection was started by my old man, so...

07:09.690 --> 07:13.030
Oh, but I collected more of
these than he did, of course.

07:13.030 --> 07:17.030
I've got all the guns here
cataloged in a database.

07:17.030 --> 07:19.030
Let's see... Guess I'll fire it up now.

07:19.030 --> 07:21.370
Uh, never mind that. The phone?

07:21.370 --> 07:24.070
Oh, that. Over there.

07:25.440 --> 07:27.030
Thanks.

07:28.380 --> 07:31.580
But I don't want you to get the wrong idea.

07:31.580 --> 07:33.710
I'm not a gun fanatic.

07:33.710 --> 07:34.980
I collected all these

07:34.980 --> 07:39.950
to deliver the iron hammer
of justice to this world of ours.

07:39.950 --> 07:43.660
There's actually a guy who's cozy
with some politicians near here, too.

07:43.660 --> 07:46.420
Hey, would you be quiet?!

07:48.900 --> 07:53.130
Your friend's got a bit of a temper.

07:53.130 --> 07:55.900
Maybe she's not getting enough calcium.

07:55.900 --> 07:57.890
Calcium?

08:03.110 --> 08:04.980
Wait five minutes.

08:12.820 --> 08:17.690
It's a gun called Colt Government M1911A1.

08:17.690 --> 08:20.860
It takes.45 caliber bullets and holds 7 rounds.

08:20.860 --> 08:23.300
Ever since it was first adopted in 1911,

08:23.300 --> 08:24.870
it's served the US Army

08:24.870 --> 08:27.540
as the standard-issue sidearm
for nearly a century.

08:27.540 --> 08:29.800
It's a famous gun.

08:29.800 --> 08:33.940
Lately, European 9mms that pack
more rounds are the mainstream,

08:33.940 --> 08:35.980
but with the rash of terrorist incidents,

08:35.980 --> 08:40.880
it's gained renewed respect for
its close-range stopping power.

08:40.880 --> 08:45.790
W-Well, I guess this might not
be very interesting to a girl...

08:45.790 --> 08:46.990
But you know,

08:46.990 --> 08:49.690
the short recoil action that
Browning developed is...

08:49.690 --> 08:51.290
It's the same as Nadie's.

08:51.290 --> 08:52.780
What?

08:58.970 --> 09:00.970
Want me to lend you a hand?

09:00.970 --> 09:02.370
Huh?

09:02.370 --> 09:06.140
You're being chased by bounty
hunters and you're in trouble, right?

09:06.140 --> 09:10.180
I may not look like much, but I know
a thing or two about marksmanship.

09:10.180 --> 09:11.480
Besides, to be honest,

09:11.480 --> 09:15.580
I doubt a woman like you is
capable of handling that thing.

09:15.580 --> 09:18.320
All I want you to lend me is your phone.

09:18.320 --> 09:20.820
Come on, you say that, but...

09:20.820 --> 09:22.480
Nadie.

09:31.200 --> 09:33.670
I take back everything I just said.
Lend me your ammo, too.

09:33.670 --> 09:35.670
Huh?

09:35.670 --> 09:37.500
And your vehicle!

09:41.180 --> 09:45.780
Wh-Who the hell are they?!
Are they out of their minds?!

09:45.780 --> 09:47.750
Find something to hang on to!

09:59.230 --> 10:03.860
They are clearly acting in
defiance of the Council's decision.

10:03.860 --> 10:05.530
Chairwoman,

10:05.530 --> 10:07.540
the Council should be convened immediately

10:07.540 --> 10:09.940
and appropriate steps taken.

10:09.940 --> 10:13.210
I understand what you are saying.

10:13.210 --> 10:17.310
However, it is currently night over there.

10:17.310 --> 10:18.710
You can't mean...

10:18.710 --> 10:21.050
They're using that to shield themselves?

10:21.050 --> 10:26.080
To us, that is our greatest governing principle.

10:30.760 --> 10:33.490
The night belongs to the witches.

10:33.490 --> 10:37.760
It is an unfettered time of freedom.

10:49.740 --> 10:52.310
- Take my place!
- Why me?!

10:52.310 --> 10:54.980
They're not after me to start
with anyway, they're after...

10:54.980 --> 10:56.950
Then, Ellis.

10:56.950 --> 10:58.590
Yessir.

10:58.590 --> 11:00.140
Hold on.

11:01.520 --> 11:05.090
I can't let you endanger yourself.

11:05.090 --> 11:07.830
Besides, this is my vehicle.

11:07.830 --> 11:11.470
There's no doubt I'm the one who
can get it to perform at its best.

11:11.470 --> 11:13.990
I don't care either way, just hurry up!

11:17.840 --> 11:20.980
The true form of the Silver Wolf...

11:20.980 --> 11:22.970
Now's the time to reveal it!

11:26.550 --> 11:28.350
What do you mean by that?

11:28.350 --> 11:29.950
It means that for several more hours,

11:29.950 --> 11:33.320
you'll have bullets raining
down on you intermittently.

11:33.320 --> 11:35.320
This isn't some weather forecast.

11:35.320 --> 11:37.960
But there's one thing I can tell you

11:37.960 --> 11:40.860
more accurately than a weather forecast.

11:42.130 --> 11:44.670
This rain...

11:44.670 --> 11:47.370
...will cease at the first light of dawn.

11:47.370 --> 11:49.970
I'll guarantee you that.

11:49.970 --> 11:52.840
So find a way to run and hold
out against them until dawn.

11:52.840 --> 11:54.330
Do you underst...

11:57.480 --> 11:59.810
Until dawn?

12:10.060 --> 12:13.420
How many hours away do you think that is?!

12:29.540 --> 12:32.610
That is a problem.

12:32.610 --> 12:36.680
Certainly, that is provided for in our contract,

12:36.680 --> 12:38.450
but this is an emergency.

12:38.450 --> 12:40.720
Can't something be done about this?

12:40.720 --> 12:44.590
No, I can't move right now.

12:51.370 --> 12:53.230
You'll be okay.

12:57.970 --> 13:01.280
Well, I suppose I'll leave it to him, then.

13:01.280 --> 13:04.440
I hardly think he's taking
a wait-and-see approach.

13:25.970 --> 13:28.270
A-According to witness accounts,

13:28.270 --> 13:33.000
the two women who were being
attacked left the city in a car.

13:34.740 --> 13:38.780
Ah, I've finally caught up to you,

13:38.780 --> 13:40.680
Ellis.

13:40.680 --> 13:43.950
That's all I know.

13:43.950 --> 13:46.950
S-So...

13:46.950 --> 13:50.650
Ellis, I'll be right there.

14:06.610 --> 14:09.170
Looks like we've got a bit of a reprieve.

14:17.120 --> 14:20.290
Hey, you.

14:20.290 --> 14:22.190
Don't you have a map?

14:27.330 --> 14:32.130
This vehicle's set up so we can look
at satellite images on the internet

14:32.130 --> 14:34.360
of any place in the world.

14:36.040 --> 14:38.140
Huh?

14:38.140 --> 14:40.710
We can't look at it?

14:40.710 --> 14:42.970
Oh, my God!

14:46.050 --> 14:48.650
I can't access the internet...

14:48.650 --> 14:50.380
What am I supposed to do?!

14:50.380 --> 14:52.820
Is it such a big deal?

14:52.820 --> 14:54.980
Any normal maps?

14:57.590 --> 14:59.490
Now that's a big deal.

14:59.490 --> 15:01.330
It's all over!

15:01.330 --> 15:03.330
We're finished!

15:03.330 --> 15:04.730
But you know...

15:04.730 --> 15:07.030
After being shot up as much as we were,

15:07.030 --> 15:10.000
almost none of the bullets have gotten through,

15:10.000 --> 15:13.240
so I guess this vehicle's made pretty rugged.

15:13.240 --> 15:15.010
What?

15:15.010 --> 15:17.950
And it's even armored in the front.

15:17.950 --> 15:20.880
Did you make the modifications
yourself, by any chance?

15:20.880 --> 15:23.180
Yeah, pretty much.

15:23.180 --> 15:26.420
It should be about as
bulletproof as an armored car.

15:26.420 --> 15:28.850
Wow, that's incredible!

15:33.430 --> 15:35.030
Incredible! Incredible!

15:35.030 --> 15:37.030
We should still be fine at this rate.

15:37.030 --> 15:39.870
We'll be fine, we'll be fine!

15:39.870 --> 15:41.860
You think so, too?

15:50.880 --> 15:52.650
If we take the right here,

15:52.650 --> 15:54.650
there's a town that got
sealed off a couple years ago

15:54.650 --> 15:56.920
because of a mysterious epidemic.

15:56.920 --> 15:59.590
Then I guess we have no choice but to go left.

15:59.590 --> 16:01.990
Even though I feel like we
may end up getting ambushed...

16:01.990 --> 16:04.750
- Right.
- Huh?

16:09.560 --> 16:11.070
Right.

16:11.070 --> 16:12.730
Ellis...

16:12.730 --> 16:15.140
Okay, let's go right.

16:15.140 --> 16:16.900
What?!

16:16.900 --> 16:19.410
We just have to hold off until dawn, right?

16:19.410 --> 16:21.680
In that case, we should try to outsmart them

16:21.680 --> 16:25.240
and take the route that might
let us buy a little extra time.

16:46.600 --> 16:50.000
- They're here.
- Why were they waiting for us over here?

16:54.110 --> 16:56.280
U-turn. We'll take the left at that fork.

16:56.280 --> 16:57.540
Straight.

16:57.540 --> 16:59.640
Hey, Ellis!

17:01.820 --> 17:04.120
Straight.

17:04.120 --> 17:07.450
Got it. We'll plow straight through.

17:07.450 --> 17:09.450
Ortega!

17:17.230 --> 17:18.570
It fell off.

17:18.570 --> 17:20.970
One plate is no big deal!

17:27.540 --> 17:29.680
I-It hit my face...

17:29.680 --> 17:31.310
It's just a scratch.

17:31.310 --> 17:33.410
5cm off and it would've been instant death!

17:33.410 --> 17:36.550
No, 3cm... Even if it'd been off by 2cm!

17:36.550 --> 17:38.050
Calm down.

17:38.050 --> 17:39.420
Let's surrender.

17:39.420 --> 17:42.490
If we just surrender peacefully,
maybe they'll at least let us live!

17:42.490 --> 17:44.360
That's not the sort of people we're up against.

17:44.360 --> 17:46.260
Ellis, take the wheel.

17:46.260 --> 17:47.890
Yessir.

18:02.840 --> 18:04.240
Another one fell off.

18:04.240 --> 18:07.510
I guess that's about what you'd
expect from an amateur mod job.

18:07.510 --> 18:09.350
Amateur?!

18:23.760 --> 18:25.630
You piece of junk!

18:27.470 --> 18:29.370
It's no good.

18:42.780 --> 18:45.090
My bullets of rage...

18:45.090 --> 18:47.550
See how you like them!

18:47.550 --> 18:49.990
- Whoa...
- He's lost it.

19:01.070 --> 19:03.000
They're up there, too!

19:13.510 --> 19:15.280
Ellis...

19:15.280 --> 19:17.110
I'm here!

19:22.760 --> 19:24.160
Soon...

19:24.160 --> 19:26.180
Soon, it'll be dawn!

19:34.470 --> 19:37.270
- Hey, what's wrong?!
- The engine stalled out.

19:37.270 --> 19:38.640
What?!

19:38.640 --> 19:40.500
And we're so close!

19:51.120 --> 19:54.620
Please start, my Silver Wolf!

19:54.620 --> 19:57.320
God, give us a miracle!

20:01.130 --> 20:03.390
A miracle!

20:16.380 --> 20:18.210
They've stopped?

20:35.030 --> 20:37.160
I see.

20:37.160 --> 20:39.000
So they're safe.

21:10.130 --> 21:11.790
Ellis!

21:15.700 --> 21:17.540
Thank you, Ortega.

21:17.540 --> 21:20.940
I wish I could at least
pay for your repairs, but...

21:20.940 --> 21:22.810
I don't care about the money.

21:22.810 --> 21:25.240
I still have my old man's inheritance anyway.

21:26.780 --> 21:29.880
I-Instead of that, could I get a ki...

21:29.880 --> 21:31.650
Could I get a kiss as thanks?

21:31.650 --> 21:33.990
What?!

21:33.990 --> 21:36.050
Not you...

21:38.930 --> 21:40.730
Just on the cheek.

21:40.730 --> 21:42.400
Why don't you do it for him?

21:42.400 --> 21:44.730
It's not like it gets used up.

21:44.730 --> 21:47.390
If you say so, Nadie.

22:15.700 --> 22:19.930
So, a girl's lips have a
rough texture to them...

22:25.010 --> 22:28.680
- Do we just keep going?
- Straight.

22:28.680 --> 22:31.850
And thus, the two...

22:31.850 --> 22:34.680
...will come to learn the truth.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Owaranai natsu no you ni

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Chiranai hana no you ni

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Dakishimeta sono ude o

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Zutto hanasanaide ite yo

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Sugari-tsuite-mitemo

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
Mune wa mada chigau hakanasa de

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Toki no rizumu kazoeteru

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
Akai hoshi no yoru

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
Kiete-yuku nukumori

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
Tsunagi-tometai no yo

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
Hitomi tojita kimi o

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Akogare o kuri-kaeshi

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Doko e mo yukenaku-temo

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
Setsunasa no tachidomaru

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
Kono hito-toki ga futari no

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
Subete yo
